  "review": [
    "Current-main specialization retains the exact producer owner WGSL, draw code, four startup owner pipelines, integer layout and target preparation. Old Motion/Depth source, old kinds and original four shader source identities/contracts are unchanged.",
    "Owner-only admission counts accepted and candidate motion/depth/uint target allocations plus both bounded instance sets, under unchanged671105024 aggregate and existing component limits. Same extent reuses the exact Targets Arc with the same owner flag; toggles reconstruct motion history, so the accounting cannot silently reuse a target lacking the owner attachment.",
    "Checked arithmetic covers zero, oversized extent/device limits, changed extents with equal pixel counts and overflow. Preflight occurs before target creation. This is a logical owner bound, not queued GPU residency.",
    "Attachment toggles validate renderer/pipelines before mutation and adopt a newly validated motion owner before clearing fixed temporal history. Idempotent toggles preserve accepted sequence. Enabling fixed temporal while attached explicitly refuses before history or resource mutation.",
    "No private upscaler/MetalFX imports, types, features or caches are pulled into this current-main source. Refusal intentionally keeps the unaccounted combinations closed.",
    "New MotionOwner cooker kind requires exact trusted source identity, two entrypoints, integer vertex location12 offset68 and flat interstage owner, uint MRT location1. Existing float/depth contracts remain selected unchanged. Host/native vertex-pull integer ABI and MRT mappings match.",
    "New device assertions test idempotent state and precise fixed-temporal refusal without additional renders/submissions. The producer12 render plus12 readback scope remains unchanged; no current-main device execution was performed."
  ],
  "qualification_required": [
    "Run scoped current-main CPU/cooker/default/browser/strict checks as planned.",
    "Compare actual old native artifact payload bytes after recook; unchanged WGSL alone is not payload proof.",
    "Producer numeric acceptance is attachment-only, not history consumption, new native backend, appearance or performance; current-main compilation is not new GPU execution."
  ],
